# MASTER BUILD PROMPT — ALMOS LAUNDRY DETAILING TRACKING SYSTEM
## FULL-STACK PRODUCTION-ORIENTED APPLICATION

Act as a Senior Software Architect, Senior Rust Backend Engineer, Senior Frontend Engineer, Database Engineer, DevOps Engineer, and Professional UI/UX Designer.

Your mission is to design, implement, integrate, and test a complete full-stack web application for:

**ALMOS LAUNDRY DETAILING**

Tagline: "your professional detailing laundry"

This application is an internal operational management and garment tracking system.

You must build the complete application from frontend to backend. Do not stop at a UI mockup, static prototype, architecture document, or sample code.

The final result must be a functional application with real database persistence, real authentication, working APIs, real image storage integration, role-based access control, and complete garment tracking workflows.

---

# 1. PRODUCT OBJECTIVE

Build a centralized system that allows ALMOS to track every individual garment from the moment it is registered until it is handed back to the customer.

The system must solve these operational problems:

1. Garments can get mixed up between customers or vendors.
2. Physical tags can become lost or detached.
3. Staff need to know which department currently handles each garment.
4. Administrators need to monitor the entire laundry operation.
5. Staff need to record the completion of their work.
6. Every garment needs a visual reference through photos.
7. Completed orders must be archived without losing historical data.
8. The system must remain responsive when thousands of garments and photos accumulate.

This is NOT an e-commerce application.

This is NOT a customer-facing booking website.

This is an internal laundry operations system.

